// edit the generators, not this file). H3b also patches four H3a
// maps with honest east doors: fortree gains the east road to
// Route 120, r111 gains the Dune Tomb mouth in its desert zone,
// r105 gains the Sea Tomb islet, r118 gains the south-east
// branch to Route 123.
// Travel law (east): the walking/surf chain fortree -> r120 ->
// r121 -> lilycove -> r124 -> mossdeep is connected end-to-end;
// mossdeep fans out to r125 (Ebbtide Cave bay) and r126; the south
// sea loop r126 -> r127 -> r128 -> r134 -> evergrande and the
// Driftlog loop r126 -> r129 -> r130 -> r131 (pacifidlog +
// Tempest Tower) -> r132 -> r133 -> r134 (currents dressed on
// 132-134) close the region's water ring. Perennial's Victory
// Road is a through-passage from the south town to the league
// plateau on the same map. Craterlake has NO surface gate: it is
// reached only from below (see DIVE PAIRS) or by air (H4 story).
// DIVE PAIRS (coordinator ruling 5, data half — the gated
// sysInteract engine is H4's): the exported DIVE_PAIRS table below
// is the machine-readable pairing list. Each entry:
//   { surface: <map id>, surfaceTile: {x, y},
//     underwater: <map id>, underwaterTile: {x, y} }
// The surfaceTile is a 'W' (dark-water) tile on the surface map,
// which ALSO carries it in its `diveSpots` list as
// {x, y, to: {map: <underwater>, x, y}} where (x, y) is the
// underwater map's landing tile (one step south of its return
// tile). The underwaterTile is an 'Ā' (waterglow) tile on the
// underwater map, which ALSO carries it in its `surfaceSpots`
// list as {x, y, to: {map: <surface>, x, y}} where (x, y) is the
// surface map's landing tile (one step south of its dive tile).
// Every underwater map carries `underwater: true` and no weather
// field. Returns are unconditional by construction: every
// surfaceSpot is a plain data link back, gated on nothing. The
// Sunken Cavern is NOT a dive pair: its mouth is a walking warp
// inside r128-underwater (and its exit warps straight back).
// Gym interiors are layouts only (leaders/battles: Stage H4);
// contest halls are dressed, NPC-free floors with a `contestHall`
// field (H5's seam) — Lotus Cove's is the fourth hall. The Regi
// tombs (desert-ruins / island-cave / ancient-tomb) ship EMPTY of
// wild encounters: dressing + sealed chamber only (tenants: H6).
// Weather is declared per outdoor map (ruling 4, data only):
// rain on 120/121 (+ the H3a rain country), sun on the south-east
// seas and Perennial, clear elsewhere east; underwater maps
